## Context

Execute the redesigned experimental matrix from 0153, after 0150
preregistration and 0144 / 0139 prerequisite fixes. Generate the
data that supports or falsifies the argument's hypotheses.

Discipline: decision rules are pre-registered. Verdicts are
recorded honestly. Falsifications are documented, not buried.

## Actions

1. Test one before blasting: dry-run + 1 real call per regime
   (`workflow.md` rule). Inspect output tokens, wall time, content
   quality. Then full sweeps.
2. Run cloud sweeps first (lower wall-time risk; results inform
   local-sweep model selection).
3. Run local sweeps on Padme. Budget agentic-loop wall-time
   conservatively (10–30 min/query for 24–32B reasoning models;
   3 reps × N queries can exceed 24h).
4. After each sweep: extract metrics, regenerate figures, update
   `hypotheses.md` with the supported / falsified / inconclusive
   verdict. No p-hacking — apply the pre-registered decision rule.
5. Where a hypothesis is falsified: short post-mortem in
   `docs/findings.md` and an honest update to `argument.md`.
6. After all sweeps: regenerate the report PDF (`make`).
   Reproducibility check: `make` from a clean tree rebuilds
   `report.pdf` without manual intervention.

## Exit criteria

- All confirmatory hypotheses have a verdict in
  `docs/hypotheses.md`.
- All figures regenerate from current data (no manual edits to
  generated artefacts).
- Falsifications documented in `docs/findings.md`; `argument.md`
  updated honestly where claims did not survive.
- `make` rebuilds `report.pdf` cleanly from current tree.
